  "description": "Lim Mun-Yeong runs into his high school first love, Yeon Hae-Jeong, in an unexpected place. And not just anywhere—as an executive at a major corporation and a janitor at that same company. It’s been ten years since he gave up on his unrequited love. Whether Hae-Jeong recognized Mun-Yeong, who was hiding his name and pretending not to know him or not, Hae-Jeong drags him around, making him do odd jobs under all sorts of childish pretexts. Although Hae-Jeong’s strange behavior, as if he somehow remembered him, made him uncomfortable, Mun-Yeong didn’t care because he no longer had any feelings for him.\n\n*“You don’t still like me, do you, Lim Mun-Yeong?”*\n\nThat is, until he heard those words from Hae-Jeong.\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
